-**Steps:**
-1. **Absolute Value:** Compute $q = |p|$, i.e., $q_x = |p_x|, q_y = |p_y|, q_z = |p_z|$ [S1, S2, unofficial]. This exploits octant symmetry.
-2. **Reflection (Fundamental Domain):** Define constant vector $k = (-\cos(\pi/6), \sin(\pi/6), \tan(\pi/6)) \approx (-0.8660254, 0.5, 0.57735)$ [S1, unofficial]. Compute $dot = k_x q_x + k_y q_y$ [S1, unofficial]. If $dot < 0$, reflect: $q_x \leftarrow q_x - 2 \cdot dot \cdot k_x$ and $q_y \leftarrow q_y - 2 \cdot dot \cdot k_y$ [S1, unofficial]. This folds the hexagon into a 30° fundamental sector [S1, unofficial].
-3. **2D Hexagon Distance:** Calculate the distance to the hexagonal cross-section in the XY plane [S1, unofficial]. Using the reflected point, compute the distance to the top edge segment: $d_{xy} = \text{length}(\max(q_x - \text{clamp}(q_x, -k_z h_x, k_z h_x), 0), \max(q_y - h_x, 0)) \cdot \text{sign}(q_y - h_x)$ [S1, unofficial].
-4. **3D Prism Distance:** Combine with the Z-axis distance $d_z = q_z - h_y$ [S1, S2, unofficial]. Return $d = \min(\max(d_{xy}, d_z), 0) + \text{length}(\max(d_{xy}, d_z, 0))$ [S1, unofficial]. Alternatively, for a flat-topped orientation, [S2, unofficial] uses $d = \max(d_z, \max(q_x \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} + q_y \cdot \frac{1}{2}, q_y) - h_x)$ [S2, unofficial].
+**Method (Source [S1, unofficial] - Folding Approach):**
+1.  Compute absolute value of point: $q = |p|$.
+2.  Reflect $q$ into the fundamental domain of the hexagon. The hexagon has 6-fold symmetry. The folding vector $k_{xy} = (-\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}, \frac{1}{2})$ defines the reflection axis.
+    -   Calculate projection factor: $t = 2 \cdot \max(0, -\text{dot}(k_{xy}, q_{xy}))$.
+    -   Update $q_{xy} \leftarrow q_{xy} + t \cdot k_{xy}$.
+3.  Compute distance to the hexagonal cross-section $d_{xy}$:
+    -   Clamp $q_x$ to the range $[-k_z h_x, k_z h_x]$. Let $c_x = \text{clamp}(q_x, -k_z h_x, k_z h_x)$.
+    -   $d_{xy} = \text{length}(q_{xy} - (c_x, h_x)) - h_x \cdot \text{sign}(q_y - h_x)$.
+    -   *Note*: This formula calculates the distance to the nearest edge or vertex of the hexagon in the folded domain.
+4.  Compute distance to the caps $d_z = q_z - h_y$.
+5.  Combine using extruded shape formula:
+    $$d = \min(\max(d_{xy}, d_z), 0) + \text{length}(\max(d_{xy}, d_z, 0))$$
 
